{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TuNdG4Mhez2k3xCvn2ap5b","type":"tool_result","content":"===\nWI-281: align smoke-budget enforcement documentation\n\nDocument the report-only local default and CI's deliberate enforced wall-clock budget, resolving the review inconsistency.\n\nWI: WI-281\n\nTrain: p0-g3-WI-281-9ae9\n\nBase: a4191b27a19640fe78ba44abeb233a4f380a6f8a\n\n===\nWI-281: rework review A — green Windows commit bar + enforce the CI wall-clock budget\n\nAddresses the two in-scope findings from review A (OPENAI, CHANGES-REQUESTED);\nthe other two are integrator/owner close-out barred to a train-branch worker.\n\nFinding 1 (Windows smoke red) — the re-tier had kept test_session_stdin in the\nbar, and its codex-lastmsg test fails on a Windows checkout: run_session's\nbatch-shim guard refuses a .cmd launcher that carries no {prompt} at all. That\nis a real guard bug and WI-275's open subject (fails identically on the\nintegration base), not fixable from this re-tiering WI. Took the reviewer's\nnamed in-scope alternative and re-tiered the whole module — a run_session\nsubprocess/shim-transport module that hosts those reds — into\nconftest.SLOW_MODULES (module-granular, like every entry). It still runs at\nclose + CI, where the full suite exposes the red for WI-275; the per-commit bar\nis now green on every supported OS. No test deleted or weakened.\n\nFinding 2 (CI wall-clock ran --mode warn, so over-budget exited 0) — the\nsmoke-budget lane now runs --mode enforce. The build session chose warn fearing\na hard time-assert would flake on fewer-core runners; re-measuring across worker\ncounts disproved it — the re-tiered tier is startup-dominated, not core-bound\n(~7.5 s/24, ~8.1 s/4, ~10.5 s/2 cores, 3.11.9), so 60 s keeps ~5x headroom and\nenforce is safe. warn→enforce strengthens the gate (not the \"weakening\" the\nfinding guarded against), so no spec-change approval was needed. The\ndeterministic membership ratchet stays the machine-independent floor in the main\ntest job. --mode warn remains the report-only local default.\n\nFindings 3 (status.md \"~3.3 min\" prose) and 4 (row done + Deliverable + spec\narchive) are root-coordination-truth edits the worker contract bars on a train\nbranch (agent_loop.py NEVER-edit list; SR-060) — deferred to the integrator's\n_rewrite_wi_rows/status regen at integration. Both findings carry -> @owner.\n\nDeclared surfaces updated in scope: pytest.ini header, conftest WI-122 block,\ndocs/stack.ini [smoke-budget] comment, session-protocol §3 (all 3 copies byte-\nidentical), and the WI-281 spec close notes + a Review A rework section.\n\nEvidence (3.11.9, 24 cores): commit bar green — `-m smoke -n auto` 349 passed\nin 7.48s (Windows; was 365 passed/1 failed pre-re-tier), check_docs 0 broken,\nruff format+lint clean, enforce check 8.3s within 60s. Full suite unchanged:\n1377 passed, 5 skipped, 2 failed (0:06:54) — the 2 failures are the known\nWI-275 Windows batch-shim reds, both now in the slow tier (off the commit bar,\non at close + CI), nothing lost.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nWI: WI-281\nTrain: p0-g3-WI-281-9ae9\nBase: a4191b27a19640fe78ba44abeb233a4f380a6f8a\n\n===","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"60090fca-712f-427b-a02a-d8755137e48f","uuid":"cf93bed3-0edb-4fe9-b9d5-f992a237a97e","timestamp":"2026-07-23T11:04:02.082Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"===\nWI-281: align smoke-budget enforcement documentation\n\nDocument the report-only local default and CI's deliberate enforced wall-clock budget, resolving the review inconsistency.\n\nWI: WI-281\n\nTrain: p0-g3-WI-281-9ae9\n\nBase: a4191b27a19640fe78ba44abeb233a4f380a6f8a\n\n===\nWI-281: rework review A — green Windows commit bar + enforce the CI wall-clock budget\n\nAddresses the two in-scope findings from review A (OPENAI, CHANGES-REQUESTED);\nthe other two are integrator/owner close-out barred to a train-branch worker.\n\nFinding 1 (Windows smoke red) — the re-tier had kept test_session_stdin in the\nbar, and its codex-lastmsg test fails on a Windows checkout: run_session's\nbatch-shim guard refuses a .cmd launcher that carries no {prompt} at all. That\nis a real guard bug and WI-275's open subject (fails identically on the\nintegration base), not fixable from this re-tiering WI. Took the reviewer's\nnamed in-scope alternative and re-tiered the whole module — a run_session\nsubprocess/shim-transport module that hosts those reds — into\nconftest.SLOW_MODULES (module-granular, like every entry). It still runs at\nclose + CI, where the full suite exposes the red for WI-275; the per-commit bar\nis now green on every supported OS. No test deleted or weakened.\n\nFinding 2 (CI wall-clock ran --mode warn, so over-budget exited 0) — the\nsmoke-budget lane now runs --mode enforce. The build session chose warn fearing\na hard time-assert would flake on fewer-core runners; re-measuring across worker\ncounts disproved it — the re-tiered tier is startup-dominated, not core-bound\n(~7.5 s/24, ~8.1 s/4, ~10.5 s/2 cores, 3.11.9), so 60 s keeps ~5x headroom and\nenforce is safe. warn→enforce strengthens the gate (not the \"weakening\" the\nfinding guarded against), so no spec-change approval was needed. The\ndeterministic membership ratchet stays the machine-independent floor in the main\ntest job. --mode warn remains the report-only local default.\n\nFindings 3 (status.md \"~3.3 min\" prose) and 4 (row done + Deliverable + spec\narchive) are root-coordination-truth edits the worker contract bars on a train\nbranch (agent_loop.py NEVER-edit list; SR-060) — deferred to the integrator's\n_rewrite_wi_rows/status regen at integration. Both findings carry -> @owner.\n\nDeclared surfaces updated in scope: pytest.ini header, conftest WI-122 block,\ndocs/stack.ini [smoke-budget] comment, session-protocol §3 (all 3 copies byte-\nidentical), and the WI-281 spec close notes + a Review A rework section.\n\nEvidence (3.11.9, 24 cores): commit bar green — `-m smoke -n auto` 349 passed\nin 7.48s (Windows; was 365 passed/1 failed pre-re-tier), check_docs 0 broken,\nruff format+lint clean, enforce check 8.3s within 60s. Full suite unchanged:\n1377 passed, 5 skipped, 2 failed (0:06:54) — the 2 failures are the known\nWI-275 Windows batch-shim reds, both now in the slow tier (off the commit bar,\non at close + CI), nothing lost.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nWI: WI-281\nTrain: p0-g3-WI-281-9ae9\nBase: a4191b27a19640fe78ba44abeb233a4f380a6f8a\n\n===","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
